{
    "word": "dimensionality",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "06aff1e7-1ba0-3513-922c-5115e02e965c",
                "word": "dimensionality",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "aaecc9df-bbc5-4f66-b9fa-607930ca7f54",
                        "entry_id": "06aff1e7-1ba0-3513-922c-5115e02e965c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dimensionalities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6e19525b-95ad-3835-9b75-d3152f5a3332",
                        "entry_id": "06aff1e7-1ba0-3513-922c-5115e02e965c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state or characteristic of possessing dimensions."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                        "entry_id": "06aff1e7-1ba0-3513-922c-5115e02e965c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The number of dimensions something has."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e66b759f-8648-4bf5-855f-7c122285f2c2",
                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                "text": "That is to say, it is the Analogue of Space, not in the sense in which we formerly regarded Space as the negation of Matter; but in the sense of Infinite Dimensionality, or of Dimensionality in all directions, as a vague generalization from the three spatial dimensions Length, Breadth, and Thickness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38afd2e7-75c5-48e1-97e1-b8a342a5a885",
                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                "text": "This often happens, for example, when a two-dimensional solution is obtained for data whose appropriate dimensionality is higher."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bfee8fb-8ada-4ba6-9d1f-776ec4b2e139",
                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                "text": "Finite Dimensionality of de Rham Cohomology:\nProposition 5.3.1. If the manifold M has a finite good cover, then its cohomology is finite dimensional."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "10f00722-7b17-42f7-bbdc-8ba31e7b4c54",
                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                "text": "As well as the low dimensionality of the Bloch electron states, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "81059fad-e5f7-4370-ad4e-d2bea64978c6",
                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                "text": "The difficulties in implementing classification algorithms as is, on high volume databases, derives from the increase in the number of records/instances in the database and of attributes/features in each instance (high dimensionality)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c597e9a8-1923-43aa-aacc-aec60dfcd673",
                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                "text": "The programming language does not impose any restrictions on the dimensionality of the arrays."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e6927b5-b0f5-4fae-8ae5-b3edd280e756",
                                "sense_id": "dbdc1472-14df-32cf-b983-cddff7488e8a",
                                "text": "A vector v=(22,38,52,12) defines a four-dimensional space with a point at the stated co-ordinates, and so on to any dimensionality n. Vector spaces of dimensionality greater than three are impossible to visualise directly […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d8fd5bc7-aa09-4d05-982a-1574bdc081fa",
                        "source_entry_id": "06aff1e7-1ba0-3513-922c-5115e02e965c",
                        "source_sense_description": "state or characteristic",
                        "target_lang_word": "dimensionnalité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dimensionnalité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2eeebbbc-a5b9-3b23-aac6-6294b19c72a7",
                                        "entry_id": "6ec8949a-7bef-3e67-8800-d6a1a61989aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nombre de dimensions de l’espace dans lequel vit un objet (au sens du nombre de directions indépendantes)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1928d68f-be37-4f30-a814-67d81f9c12ad",
                                                "sense_id": "2eeebbbc-a5b9-3b23-aac6-6294b19c72a7",
                                                "text": "Les physiciens sont maintenant capables de fabriquer des matériaux de basses dimensionnalités effectives : fils quantiques unidimensionnels, couches minces semi-conductrices bidimensionnelles…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a9d29379-acf5-300e-92bd-1f48e97d337d",
                                        "entry_id": "6ec8949a-7bef-3e67-8800-d6a1a61989aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dimension d’une quantité physique, en fonction des unités fondamentales (mètre, seconde…)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "92f50e95-ceba-42cb-b39b-0d2b59406adc",
                        "source_entry_id": "06aff1e7-1ba0-3513-922c-5115e02e965c",
                        "source_sense_description": "state or characteristic",
                        "target_lang_word": "Dimensionalität",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dimensionalität",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "276dd631-f4d7-3679-bed8-377fea5df25d",
                                        "entry_id": "c4591def-6b34-3a75-8091-81d8b87e0b86",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Eigenschaft/Beschaffenheit Ausdehnung (auf verschiedenen Ebenen und/oder in verschiedene Richtungen, Dimensionen) zu haben; gerade im Plural auch synonym mit Dimension verwendet"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94a54714-32b5-46fc-b07a-76a99d5ba7fe",
                                                "sense_id": "276dd631-f4d7-3679-bed8-377fea5df25d",
                                                "text": "„Tatsächlich lassen sich wesentliche Aspekte dieser Begriffsvielfalt ordnen, indem grundsätzlich zwischen drei Stufen der Dimensionalität von Raum, und zwei Qualitäten von Raum unterschieden wird.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65f09110-5fda-4827-b653-0b38d5151116",
                                                "sense_id": "276dd631-f4d7-3679-bed8-377fea5df25d",
                                                "text": "„Die Frage der notwendigen Dimensionalität war schon immer ein Lieblingsthema der Architektur.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fd9b735-a731-4caf-b96e-f4f5305681a6",
                                                "sense_id": "276dd631-f4d7-3679-bed8-377fea5df25d",
                                                "text": "„Die Ähnlichkeitsmaße können mit dem Verfahren der multidimensionalen Analyse in einen euklidischen Raum möglichst geringer Dimensionalität transponiert werden. Das Ergebnis ist eine Metrik der sozialen Distanz.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e29d4ad4-ed02-49d9-a9ec-d4bc3a4144e0",
                                                "sense_id": "276dd631-f4d7-3679-bed8-377fea5df25d",
                                                "text": "„Eine andere Erklärung wäre, dass die Items gar nicht das Gleiche messen, die tatsächlichen Unterscheidungen der Befragten also eine andere Dimensionalität aufweisen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7a9059a-92e7-44a1-8507-fd84c8e77133",
                                                "sense_id": "276dd631-f4d7-3679-bed8-377fea5df25d",
                                                "text": "„Mit ihm werden, im übrigen darin dem »Ich« sehr verwandt, jeweils ganz eigene Dimensionalitäten aufgeblendet. Ein »transzendentales Ich« beschreibt eine völlig andere Ebene als das »empirische Ich«.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55042556-178d-429e-933f-995aae040747",
                                                "sense_id": "276dd631-f4d7-3679-bed8-377fea5df25d",
                                                "text": "„Mit Dimensionalität bezeichnet man die Zahl der Freiheitsgrade der Bewegung eines technischen Objektes, auf die der Operateur mit den Bedienelementen Einfluß nehmen kann.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
